      "point": "Britannica gives only a cross-reference with no historical detail, while Wikipedia provides extensive history",
      "quote_britannica": "BYZANTIUM, the ancient name of Confiantinople. See COMPENTINORY.",
      "quote_wikipedia": "Byzantium (/ b ɪ ˈ z æ n t i ə m, - ʃ ə m /) or Byzantion (Ancient Greek: Βυζάντιον) was an ancient Greek city in classical antiquity that became known as Constantinople in late antiquity and Istanbul in modern times."
    },
