      "point": "Britannica does not mention the Ottoman conquest of 1453, while Wikipedia does",
      "quote_britannica": "BYZANTIUM, the ancient name of Confiantinople. See COMPENTINORY.",
      "quote_wikipedia": "On May 29, 1453, the city was conquered by the Ottoman Turks, and again became the capital of a powerful state, the Ottoman Empire."
    },
    {
      "point": "Britannica does not mention the etymology or the founder Byzas, while Wikipedia does",
      "quote_britannica": "BYZANTIUM, the ancient name of Confiantinople. See COMPENTINORY.",
      "quote_wikipedia": "The etymology of Byzantium is unknown. It has been suggested that the name is of Thracian origin."
    },
    {
      "point": "Britannica does not mention the star and crescent symbol, while Wikipedia does",
      "quote_britannica": "BYZANTIUM, the ancient name of Confiantinople. See COMPENTINORY.",
      "quote_wikipedia": "By the late Hellenistic or early Roman period (1st century BC), the star and crescent motif was associated to some degree with Byzantium"
    }
  ],
  "claims": [
